{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Anger</b> — \"will plead my cause\": from the nations." "<b>Will bring me out to light</b> — the opposite of \"for I sit in darkness.\" And the meaning of \"I will see as His light [illuminates] my heart\" [is]: then I will understand that HaShem is righteous concerning all that comes upon me, or I will see in His righteousness that He will take my vengeance from my enemy."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:15.300115958Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}